    "scope": "Surviving Eanna/Inanna ziggurat constituent of the named Eanna district: mapped irregular lower perimeter, eroded stepped brick core, broad broken shelves, runoff gullies and uneven open crown. No restored summit temple, intact ancient staircase or invented precinct-room grid. Other Eanna remains stay host terrain.",
    "constructionStatus": "continuous-authoring-and-inspection",
    "identityBasis": "Candidate Q706970 is the Eanna temple complex; its broad reference point is about454m southwest of the standard named Eanna District point35185683624246 and Ziggurat of Uruk point35185683624247. Model only that explicitly reviewed Eanna/Inanna ziggurat constituent at the two overlapping building controls35185683624247/248. Their mapped present-day lower/core outlines fix about74x70m native extent. Native east/south at heading0; mapped architectural axis about0.828849rad, without a signed doorway-facing claim. Broader precinct and other temples are not authored.",
    "heightBasis": "About9.6m exposed core above local standard terrain with a low0.85m perimeter remnant. Picture-led height, shelf survival, gully depths, crown level and minor broken ledges are approximate. The model does not restore ancient stages or the vanished summit temple.",
    "terrainBasis": "Retain the pinned standard Protomaps2026-10-14/Mapzen13–14 six-meter native grid and independent buildings. Lower perimeter and core feet follow sampled grade with buried bottoms; elevated relief is authored exposed masonry/eroded brick, not a copied DEM-only mound. Preserve ground and water; replace only two corresponding native procedural shells with2cm numeric margin. No flattened precinct or ground/water cutout."
